{
  "kanji": "顔",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 顔\ntitle: face; expression\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-2, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 18\nradical: 頁\nradicalNumber: 181\nonyomi: [ガン]\nkunyomi: [かお]\ndistractors: [願, 題, 類]\n---\n\n# 顔 — face; expression\n\n**Strokes:** 18 · **Key (radical):** 頁 (no. 181) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n顔 is the face and, by extension, the expression visible on it.\nThe ordinary noun is [顔](../words/顔.md) かお; 笑顔 (えがお) means a smiling face or smile.\n顔を洗います。 (かおをあらいます。) — I wash my face.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** distinguish the left 彦-shaped block, with its three slanting strokes,\nfrom the right 頁. Imagine the slanting strokes drawing attention to someone's face.\nThis is a modern visual cue, not historical derivation.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| かお | kun | [顔](../words/顔.md) かお — face |\n| ガン | on | 顔面 がんめん — face |\n\nIn 笑顔 (えがお), 顔 is voiced to がお; learn the whole word's reading.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [顔](../words/顔.md) かお — face\n- 笑顔 えがお — smile; smiling face\n- 顔面 がんめん — face\n\n## Notes\n\n[面](面.md) also has a face sense, alongside \"surface\" and \"mask\"; the whole word helps identify the intended meaning.\n[願](願.md) has 原 on the left rather than 彦.\n[題](題.md) and [類](類.md) share only the right 頁 block with 顔.\n\nDictionary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1217730, 1217860, 1351400, 1489700.\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\n",
